Parallel zlib encoding

Compress zlib rectangle strips independently (raw deflate, reset for every
strip) in multiple threads, sending them in order as soon as they're ready.
Independently compressed strips ending with a sync flush form a valid
continuation of the client's zlib stream - zlib header is sent once per
client. Strips are compressed directly from framebuffer if no pixel format
translation is needed.

Strips are compressed with libdeflate (patched to end its output with a sync
flush, and with a faster mode for 32-bit pixels), if the CPU supports NEON -
it compresses video as well as zlib-ng level 2 in a third of the time.

