  * zlib.c
  *
  * Routines to implement zlib based encoding (deflate).
+ *
+ * Rectangles are split into strips, which are compressed in parallel by
+ * multiple threads, each strip independently of previous data (raw deflate
+ * stream reset for every strip), and then sent in order. Since every strip
+ * ends with a sync flush, the strips form a valid continuation of the client's
+ * single zlib stream - zlib header is sent once, with the first zlib
+ * rectangle, and the stream is never finished, so its checksum is never
+ * verified by clients.
+ *
+ * Strips are compressed with libdeflate (patched to end its output with a
+ * sync flush) if the CPU supports NEON, which libdeflate is built with.
+ * libdeflate level 1, in its (patched in) mode for 32-bit pixels, compresses
+ * video about as well as zlib-ng level 2, in a third of the time. Otherwise
+ * zlib is used.
  */
 
